{"type":"message","id":"a3848dc9","parentId":"ac2ae564","timestamp":"2026-03-20T00:08:25.556Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Analyzing Discord Gateway Health**\n\nI've just confirmed the Discord Gateway's health via `discord-gateway-health.sh`, and it returned a positive status: \"healthy\". The output is: `{\"ok\": true , \"status\": \"healthy\", \"issue\": false, \"reason\": \"runtime-connected\", ...}`. This suggests the user's issue doesn't stem from direct gateway connectivity problems, though the initial message about \"Qualidade\" warrants further investigation.\n\n\n**Formulating Alert Response**\n\nI've determined the Discord Gateway is healthy based on the script's output. However, the root cause relates to a quality issue within the \"Pessoal\" Notion database as indicated by the user's initial message. I'm formulating an `ALERTA` block in pt-BR, adhering to the `HEARTBEAT.md` rules, based on this \"Qualidade Notion\" problem. I'm also noting that the \"Governança\" cron job is currently running to address these kinds of issues, so my next step is to wait for it to finish.\n\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<final>ALERTA\n- Problema: Qualidade Notion (Pessoal): 1 card.\n- Impacto: Potencial desorganização em tarefas pessoais.\n- Ação executada: Cron de governança rodando há 3min.\n- Próximo passo: Monitorar conclusão do cron. (ETA: 5min)</final>","textSignature":""}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-2.5-flash","usage":{"input":25601,"output":368,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25969,"cost":{"input":0.007680299999999999,"output":0.00092,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0086003}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773965302353}}
